# Local planning notes, agent scratch and tool state. None of this is part
# of the project, and all of it is one `git add -A` away from being
# published. Ignoring it here rather than only in .git/info/exclude means
# a fresh clone is protected too, not just the machine that set it up.
.plans/
.superpowers/
.claude/
